41708364","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2d8b-e773-8ace-46c8"},{"link_uuid":"50a87d0d-150c-442c-bea5-79c5e4c531f6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"684a-c899-d4af-45d3"}],"description":"## Observation\nDuring a compaction fold, `_build_authorship_ledger` -> `authorship.identify_signer` -> `_keyring_for` -> `rebar.show_ticket` -> `ensure_fresh` runs while `_compact_locked` holds the store write lock. When the 60 s freshness marker has expired, `ensure_fresh` runs `git fetch` (network in production) and then `sync.reconverge`, which requests the same store write lock the fold already holds. It waits out its 2 s pass against its own process, then gives up.\n\nMeasured on a clone of `tickets` at `daa3a65239b^` with a local mirror as `origin` (2026-11-03, `origin/main` `25bce6c0550`): first signed fold `ensure_fresh` 2.22 s, nested lock wait 2.04 s, fetch 0.11 s (local mirror; production fetches over the network). Evidence on `breezelike-travelsick-moray`.\n\n## Expected\nA locked critical section never fetches and never requests a lock it already holds. Keyring lookups for the ledger read local state, or run before the lock like `preresolve_unmapped_positions`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A fold with signed events runs no `git fetch` and no store-lock acquisition while `_compact_locked` holds the lock (test observes the lock dir at each call).\n- [ ] The authorship ledger is unchanged for the same input.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2d8b-e773-8ace-46c8"],["relates_to","684a-c899-d4af-45d3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b29c0d61-113d-4516-ad7a-3c369db3f6e1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1ae0-ff59-b62e-4267","ticket_